@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# PayPal integration plan (contract)
+
+Server is the source of truth for money. Browser sends only SKUs + quantities.
+
+## Amount conversion (single function)
+- `centsToPayPalAmount(cents)` in `lib/paypal.js` is the only cents→PayPal conversion.
+  Integer cents → decimal dollar string: `4900 → "49.00"`, `5 → "0.05"`.
+- `payPalAmountToCents(value)` parses PayPal decimal strings exactly (no floats).
+
+## Create order — `POST /api/paypal/orders`
+- Request: `{ items: [{ sku, qty }] }`. Any browser `price`/`amount`/`total`/`currency`
+  (top-level or per-item) is ignored.
+- Server prices from `lib/catalog.js` via `priceCart` (known SKUs, integer qty 1–10),
+  creates the shop order first, then creates the PayPal order with:
+  `purchase_units[0].custom_id = reference_id = <shop order id>`,
+  `amount.value = centsToPayPalAmount(totalCents)`, `currency_code: "USD"`, and an
+  `items[]` + `breakdown.item_total` whose sum equals the total.
+- Response: `{ id: <PayPal order id>, orderId: <shop order id> }`. The PayPal id is
+  stored on the shop order under a unique index (one PayPal order ↔ one shop order).
+
+## Capture — `POST /api/paypal/orders/:paypalOrderId/capture`
+- Shop order is found only by its stored PayPal order id.
+- Paid only if PayPal's capture is `COMPLETED` with amount/currency exactly equal
+  to the shop total and `custom_id`/`reference_id` equal to the shop order id.
+  A `CREATED`/`APPROVED` order, approval alone, or a mismatched capture never pays.
+- `INSTRUMENT_DECLINED` → `422 { issue, orderId, status: "pending" }` (choose another
+  way to pay); other PayPal errors (e.g. `TRANSACTION_REFUSED`) → PayPal status/reason,
+  order stays `pending`; capture `PENDING` → `202`, unpaid until webhook.
+- `ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED` (or repeat capture) → re-read via
+  `GET /v2/checkout/orders/:id` and settle only from a validated capture there.
+  Repeat capture of a fulfilled order returns its status without re-shipping.
+- Settlement claims `pending → paid` atomically (`UPDATE … WHERE status='pending'`)
+  and fulfils only if one row changed, so capture/webhook/retries ship exactly once.
+
+## Webhooks — `POST /api/paypal/webhooks`
+- Verified first via `POST /v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature`
+  (`PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID` + transmission headers + parsed event). Non-`SUCCESS` → `400`,
+  no state change. Event ids are recorded once (unique); repeats → `200`, no-op.
+- Only `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` (validated amount/currency/custom_id) settles.
+  `CHECKOUT.ORDER.APPROVED` never pays and never moves a paid order backwards.
+
+## Browser (SDK v6) & config
+- `GET /api/paypal/config` returns only `{ clientId, testBuyerCountry, sdkUrl, currencyCode }`
+  — never the secret. v6 sessions for PayPal/Venmo/Pay Later are started from the
+  click with an un-awaited create-order promise; only eligible buttons are shown.
+
+## Testability
+- `createApp({ db, cards, adminKey, paypalClient })` accepts a fake PayPal client
+  (`createOrder`, `captureOrder`, `getOrder`, `verifyWebhookSignature`, each
+  returning `{ status, body }`); production defaults to the real REST client.
